{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the process in the Pathology Department, begin with the Gross pathology request that has arrived."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly starts the process (init) and describes initializing and receiving the gross pathology request."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, proceed with the Registration gross pathology request."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to completing the registration step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During the \"Registration gross pathology request\" step, make sure to create a barcode scan at the start."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly describes creating the barcode scan during registration."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the registration is complete, assign a container to the gross pathology request."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly matches assigning the container post-registration."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For the \"Specimen description\" step, pay attention to the scan start. Then, pay attention to the scan end. Finally, pay attention to the scan start again for the Registration gross pathology request (cont.) step."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the sequential scan start, scan end, and follow-up scan start actions described for specimen and registration continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following that, proceed with Macroscopic description writing."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithful paraphrase of writing the macroscopic description."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10",
        "action:n17",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, complete the following steps: Tissue processing, check if \"Digitalization?\" is required."
      ],
      "justification": "The simultaneous instruction implies structural branching and convergence. The span covers the tissue processing actions and the digitalization check, which is faithfully restated as an action node per modeling conventions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n13",
        "action:n13",
        "guard:b1->n12",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the answer is \"no,\" continue the process. If the answer is \"yes,\" proceed with Digitalization."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately captures the yes/no guard conditions and their respective positive/negative flow actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18",
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, assign cases to the pathologist and then move on to Microscopic examination and diagnosis."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to assigning cases and performing the microscopic examination/diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20",
        "action:n21"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the microscopic examination and diagnosis are complete, write the pathology report. After writing the report, confirm it."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps precisely to writing and then confirming the pathology report."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n22",
        "action:n23"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the pathology report is confirmed, deliver it. Then, proceed with the post-report processing."
      ],
      "justification": "Aligns with the initial report delivery and starting post-report processing."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n24",
        "action:n25",
        "action:n26"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To conclude the pathology procedure, close it. Finally, deliver the pathology report and complete the post-report processing."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers closing the procedure, final delivery, completing post-processing, and structurally marking the process end."
    }
  ],
